oming out and  saying you know  uh you know if the ravens can't control  their covert situation that should be on  them  uh forgetting the fact that that uh two  weeks earlier the steelers had five guys  on the list including ben roethlisberger  but the timing benefited them because  they could come off on saturday and play  on sunday  beyond that i think mike tomlin's  directive to them is as  always is just hey look just keep the  focus stay on it stay on the path we're  on  and um i i you know if anything maybe  they're getting a little antsy  um but hey look the same complaints are  coming out of pittsburgh not necessarily  from the state  from the team and the players but from  their fans and maybe internally there's  some oh you know we're getting the short  end of the stick  but i don't think that that permeates  the locker room mike tomlin won't allow  that to happen  but yeah i think every team feels  they're being picked on look at the  denver broncos dan they petitioned  the league every which way they could to  try and do something about that  quarterback situation  and and it didn't happen and so yeah in  pittsburgh they think baltimore is  getting  getting an advantage in baltimore they  think they're getting screwed  when was the last time you covered a  steeler team that had  this well least dramatic steeler team  in how many years well you know  uh it's funny because every year it  seems to come up i don't think there's  any question then the two years ago  with the le'veon bell situation in the  antonio brown situation  i don't think that drama could ever be  surpassed no matter what happens  and and i think because the steelers are  such a marquee team  and as you know being in the business  they are a team that moves the needle  and because of that they receive a lot  of attention it's also because they tend  to have a lot of the game's top stars  so and go back to antonio brown and  le'veon bell so  when those situations arise they get  magnifie