yers to  talk about  i think buffalo you know once if they  can get past that in a couple weeks you  know see what happens with the ravens  then they have washington and i know  washington's been scoring some points  lately  but they are four and seven then they go  to buffalo and i think  excuse me i think that will be the key  they could be 12-0 going to buffalo  and if they come through that at 13-0  then i think it becomes a very real  possibility because  then it's then it's the colts and then  it's the you know then it's the season  ending game and let's say the buy is  still in place  nothing has changed and they get a bye  week then what do you do  in week 16 you go for an unbeaten season  or do you  you back off a little bit um you know  i've talked to a couple  former coaches around the league and  they all think it's probably a good idea  if they lose a game somewhere  i tend to agree just to get the the  specter and the pressure of an unbeaten  season off their back  and and you know then start focusing on  on the postseason so  but i i think uh i think uh two or three  weeks here when they head to buffalo is  going to be the key damn  great to talk to you jerry thanks for  making time have fun today we appreciate  it  well dan nice chatting with you jerry  dolak he covers the steelers for the  pittsburgh post gazette

